@nilvng Thanks for your continued work on this and insights into your thought process ✨ 

I've been reviewing this a bit deeper and have a few more things I'd like to address, and I also have a proposal for a refactor.

### Interactive checkouts can behave unexpectedly for fork PRs

_TLDR: we must include both `headRepository` and `maintainerCanModify` in the requested fields even though we don't display those fields to the user when they select the PR. We need to request at least the same fields as the non-interactive flow to later do the necessary Git operations_ 

While testing this, I've noticed that some PRs cause my terminal prompt to behave unexpectedly, and clue me into that the interactive flow was doing different `git` operations than the non-interactive flow:

![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c902f9a-3e37-4941-a3a5-6d0505170d9c)

This is what I'd typically expect instead:

![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c768b3fd-bcf1-4c0b-bec8-adb2f3a3e8c7)

I discovered this was because of this logic which occurs later in the process:

https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/d92e529629f2ccc0c87c4a49e0b2f199602bfb3c/pkg/cmd/pr/checkout/checkout.go#L271-L275

Since the interactive flow was not requesting these fields ( `headRepository` and `maintainerCanModify`), they were false or `nil`. This causes the the `.merge` config to be set to a reference to a pull request's head commit instead of a reference to a branch. 

**Interactive flow**

https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/d92e529629f2ccc0c87c4a49e0b2f199602bfb3c/pkg/cmd/pr/checkout/checkout.go#L321-L330

**non-interactive flow**

https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/d92e529629f2ccc0c87c4a49e0b2f199602bfb3c/pkg/cmd/pr/checkout/checkout.go#L98-L108

## Refactoring interactive flow

I'd like to propose a refactor to the logic around deciding whether to prompt. I'd like to:

- Align more closely with other command implementations by moving away from the `switch` statement for this use-case.
- Improve readability by moving more logic into `selectPR`, which I've renamed to `ResolvePR` given it's new behavior.

Note: this proposal includes solutions to the above problem regarding the `headRepository` and `maintainerCanModify` fields and solutions to [my other comment](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/9868#discussion_r1866407659) about moving the prompting check into `RunE`.

I'd like to push a commit to this PR with my proposal below, if you agree with the essence of the refactor, then we can refactor further if needed ❤️ 

Please feel free to `git apply` this diff below to your local branch and let me know what you think 😁 🙌  

Edit: here's [an example from `gh workflow enable`](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/5a74934d192ddce979ca64377be6e10af8680467/pkg/cmd/workflow/enable/enable.go#L77) that is similar to the refactor I am going for. In that case `ResolveWorkflow` handles getting a workflow from the user, and it will prompt the user if it needs to - I propose a similar idea with `resolvePR` that handles getting a PR from the user, enclosing the decision to prompt or not within that function.  

